[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi guys! I am a bit confused, because my PR (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/25978\">#25978</a>) fails in the testing stage with:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>../tools-branch/scripts/lake-build-wrapper.py .lake/build_summary_MathlibTest.json lake --iofail test<br>\nBuild progress [starting at 2033/2340]<br>\n✖ [8179/8457] Building MathlibTest.FinCoercions (4.7s)<br>\nBuild progress [starting at 8180/8457]<br>\nSome required targets logged failures:</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>MathlibTest.FinCoercions<br>\nerror: build failed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The weird thing is that I did not touch this file or anything near it, I just changed a leaf file. I would appreciate it  a lot if someone could point me to what I'm missing here. (Merging master sadly did not magically fix it)</p>",
        "id": 577596110,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1772744223
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems like the coercions you did add are slowing down type class search in some cases. Not sure I have good suggestions how to deal with that.</p>",
        "id": 577609131,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1772749360
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>How can I benchmark this? Is there a way to see what Type Class search is doing?</p>",
        "id": 577750773,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1772804219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When using <code>set_option diagnostics true</code>, i see</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>  [type_class] used instances (max: 1349, num: 5): ▼\n    [] instCoeTC ↦ 1349\n    [] instCoeTCOfCoe ↦ 1349\n    [] instCoeTCOfCoe_1 ↦ 1349\n    [] Open.instCoe ↦ 1349\n    [] Open.instFrame ↦ 1339\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What does this mean? Why is lean looking at <code>Open</code> even if <code>Fin n</code> is not a Frame?</p>",
        "id": 577752240,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1772804592
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should use <code>set_option trace.Meta.synthInstance true</code>. the <code>diagnostics</code> are not very helpful indeed.</p>",
        "id": 577759197,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1772806462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I get very deep stacks of the form:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">✅️</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instFrame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Frame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))))))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">resume</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">propagating</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Frame</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                      </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))))))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">subgoal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Frame</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                      </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))))))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)))))))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">↑</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))))))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▶</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This seems to be the result of:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Frame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getElement</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is the solution just not having this instance or is there something else that could be done? (My intution would be that Lean wouldn't care about this instance as long as <code>X</code> isn't a Frame)</p>",
        "id": 577761436,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1772807061
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is because the first parameter is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=semiOutParam#doc\">docs#semiOutParam</a>. Replacing <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Coe#doc\">docs#Coe</a> with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CoeOut#doc\">docs#CoeOut</a> should be fine.</p>",
        "id": 577762894,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuyang Zhao",
        "timestamp": 1772807429
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice, this works! Thanks a lot for pointing this out!</p>",
